WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.800
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain a Japanese psychological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:15.920
short thriller film called “Chess.”&nbsp;
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.640
In the opening scene, the World chess champion&nbsp;
Akira Kato is playing a match of chess against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.240
a computer called the Super Blue at the Special&nbsp;
Chess Exhibition. While Akira’s brain can only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.280
calculate three moves in a second, Super Blue&nbsp;
can calculate up to two hundred million moves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.720
per second. The chances of Akira’s winning seem&nbsp;
low, but if he loses, he will be the first player&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.280
in history to lose to a computer. As the intense&nbsp;
game continues, he is visibly struggling. At last,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.320
he drops his king, accepting his defeat.&nbsp;
The room goes silent and no one can believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.200
that the world’s most talented chess player,&nbsp;
who has never lost a single match, just lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.320
to a computer. Akira sits with his head down,&nbsp;
not being able to process what just happened.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.360
The host mocks him as the audience laughs&nbsp;
and reporters click pictures of a humiliated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:11.120
former “grand world champion”. Akira bangs the&nbsp;
chessboard in anger, breaking it in half.
&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.320
Three years have passed since the incident. After&nbsp;
the last match, Akira has stopped playing chess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.360
and no one has seen him ever since. The following&nbsp;
scene shows us many homeless people sitting on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.360
side of the road on a cold morning. One of them&nbsp;
is Akira who has spent all his money on alcohol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:33.600
and gambling and is now living in the streets. A&nbsp;
fancy car stops by them and two men in black suits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.360
step out of it. They forcefully pick up Akira and&nbsp;
drive him away. He is taken to a mansion where he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:45.360
is welcomed by a wealthy old man. The man reveals&nbsp;
that he knows who Akira is, which is surprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:50.720
considering he has changed his name and identity&nbsp;
entirely. When Akira inquires about who he is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:56.080
the man says it isn't important. He simply wants&nbsp;
to play a game of chess with Akira. He reveals a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:02.160
chessboard on the table which makes Akira almost&nbsp;
puke. He composes himself and makes an excuse but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:07.360
the truth is that the thought of chess makes him&nbsp;
sick at this point in life. He turns away from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:14.880
chessboard, not being able to look at it.
The old man says that he lost a lot of money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:20.000
betting on Akira’s last match. Since Akira doesn’t&nbsp;
have even a single penny, the man wants him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:25.680
play a game to compensate for the loss. Akira is&nbsp;
unsure about the man’s actual intention but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:30.480
knows he doesn’t want to do any business with him.&nbsp;
To get out of the situation, he bluntly tells the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.600
man that he doesn’t play chess anymore, moreover,&nbsp;
he doesn’t want to be a millionaire's plaything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:40.960
The man picks up the king on Akira’s side and&nbsp;
says that he has lost without even playing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:47.120
This reminds Akira of his last defeat which makes&nbsp;
him furious. He stops the man and asks him to move&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:53.200
his pawn instead. Satisfied that he has finally&nbsp;
persuaded Akira, the old man plays his move.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.560
However, Akira refuses to turn towards the&nbsp;
chessboard or touch the pieces. Without even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.800
looking, he tells the man to move all of his&nbsp;
pieces, confident that he will win the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:08.400
anyway. We notice that the old man is wearing an&nbsp;
earpiece and talking to someone while playing. 
&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:13.680
Akira walks to the window where he sees a group&nbsp;
of men downstairs wearing white and black clothes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.000
and facing each other. The pattern they are&nbsp;
standing in is exactly the same as the pattern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.720
on the chessboard right now. As the old man&nbsp;
kills one of his pawns in the game, the man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:29.200
who was in the pawn’s place is stabbed and killed.&nbsp;
Akira freezes in shock at what he just witnessed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.320
He asks the man if this is some kind of joke. The&nbsp;
man says that the pawns are mere soldiers so he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.520
shouldn’t be sad about one’s death. Akira runs&nbsp;
downstairs to check the dead person for himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:44.240
and finds him on the ground while the other&nbsp;
players stand still in their places. He takes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:49.040
knife out of the man’s body and sees that he is&nbsp;
still alive. Even on the verge of death, the man&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:54.480
smiles and asks Akira what his next move is.
After the man takes his last breath, the players&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.360
around him walk away, leaving Akira with a knife&nbsp;
and a dead body in the middle of the street.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.480
A woman sees him in the position and assumes&nbsp;
that he killed the person. Akira freaks out and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:09.680
retreats, stating that it wasn’t him. In the&nbsp;
following scene, he is at his former doctor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:15.760
Seiichi Tomoda’s office. The doctor is surprised&nbsp;
to see him after so many years. He and Akira’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:21.680
wife Kumi Kato have been looking for Akira for the&nbsp;
past three years. A flashback from three years ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:26.880
shows us that after losing the game with Super&nbsp;
Blue, Akira had lost the will to live. He used to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.920
get nightmares of chess pieces trying to kill him.&nbsp;
The nightmares turned into hallucinations which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.440
made his health even worse. He had always compared&nbsp;
his life to a game of chess and his wife was his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:43.280
queen. So, when he lost the match, he left his&nbsp;
queen, believing he didn’t deserve her anymore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:48.560
Akira tells the doctor about the incident earlier&nbsp;
and says he might be in need of a psychiatrist.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.760
The doctor assumes he dreamt of the guy being&nbsp;
killed but Akira insists what he saw was in fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:59.120
real. The doctor asks him to go home and&nbsp;
rest because his mind is still fragile. 
&nbsp;

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:04.800
Following that, a printer at the doctor’s cabin&nbsp;
prints out a paper on its own. The paper says&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.680
“what is your next move?”. Akira realizes that&nbsp;
the match of chess he started that morning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.480
is still going on. He shouts that he&nbsp;
wants his Pawn moved to the E3 position.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:19.600
Then, the doctor opens a book to see its pages&nbsp;
have turned into a chessboard. The printer prints&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:25.760
another paper that says in the next move, the old&nbsp;
man’s queen kills Akira’s knight. The knight just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:32.880
so happens to be Doctor Tomoda. He vomits blood&nbsp;
and dies instantly. Akira is left shocked when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.920
he sees a picture of the doctor riding a horse&nbsp;
on the wall, meaning the doctor was his knight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:42.960
The cup he was drinking from earlier, also has a&nbsp;
chessboard pattern, so Akira assumes the coffee&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:47.920
was drugged. A nurse watches them through the door&nbsp;
but doesn’t do anything to save the doctor. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:54.560
walks in only after he is dead and asks Akira what&nbsp;
his next move is. Akira runs outside, trembling in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:59.680
fear when he comes across a little kid holding a&nbsp;
drawing with the current format of the chessboard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:04.720
It is clear that he is also involved in the&nbsp;
game when he asks Akira the same question.
&nbsp;

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:09.840
Akira answers that he wants to move the king to&nbsp;
the E2 position. The kid tells him that the king&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:15.040
will end up dead, making Akira run in the other&nbsp;
direction. He gets a vision of people who have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.400
died because of the game and starts hallucinating&nbsp;
chess pieces trying to kill him. As he runs away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:25.440
he reaches a parking lot where the cars have been&nbsp;
parked in the format of the chessboard. Unknown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.240
to this, he gets in the car that is supposed to&nbsp;
be the bishop and tries to start it. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:36.080
similar to a bishop in chess, the car only moves&nbsp;
diagonally. He leaves that car alone and gets on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:41.040
the one that denotes the Rook. The car doesn’t&nbsp;
start because it is the opponent’s turn to play.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:48.960
The rook from the other side crashes into&nbsp;
his car, killing his rook. Following that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:54.560
Akira goes to his old house only to see that it&nbsp;
is on sale. The rook, also known as the castle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:59.600
was actually his house in real life. Now&nbsp;
that Akira gets the hang of real-life chess,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:05.680
he realizes that the queen is his wife Kumi and&nbsp;
her life is in danger as well. He goes back to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.720
old man’s home claiming that he wants to quit&nbsp;
playing the game and asking for his wife.
&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:16.880
However, the old man asks Akira to accept his&nbsp;
defeat and remove his king to end the game. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.520
again reminds Akira of the time he was humiliated&nbsp;
after losing a match with the Super blue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.760
With determination, he continues playing the&nbsp;
game and asks the old man to move his king&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:36.080
forward. The game goes on for a long time and&nbsp;
most of their pieces are out. At last, Akira is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:41.520
only two steps away from winning the game and the&nbsp;
old man can do nothing to save his king. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:46.960
before he can play his turn, two men in suits&nbsp;
forcefully take him away. In the following scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:51.520
the old man and Akira are in a stadium that&nbsp;
has a life-size chessboard in the middle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:56.000
The chess pieces are people who will die with a&nbsp;
single wrong move. The old man says that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:01.280
situation is similar to an Arabian king who used&nbsp;
to play chess with his prisoners, killing them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:05.920
on the spot. He states that chess is a game&nbsp;
without emotion because the players sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:11.200
have to sacrifice their own pieces in order to&nbsp;
win. For Akira to win the game, he will have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:17.680
to move a knight to checkmate. However, if he does&nbsp;
that, the old man will kill his queen. Akita turns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:24.080
around to see that the queen is actually his wife&nbsp;
Kumi who has been tied and held at knifepoint.
&nbsp;

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.160
With tears in her eyes, she shakes&nbsp;
her head, asking Akira to save her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:32.240
Now, Akira can either win&nbsp;
the game or lose his wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:38.160
forever. He tries to move from his box to stop&nbsp;
the man but a sniper fires close to his legs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:43.600
as a warning that moving will get him killed. The&nbsp;
old man asks him for the last time if he wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:49.360
sacrifice the queen or accept his defeat. He also&nbsp;
adds that a real champion would think logically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:54.800
and do what is needed to win the game. But Akita&nbsp;
tells them to save the queen without hesitation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.600
His wife is more important to him than winning&nbsp;
a match. Everyone is shocked at his decision.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.880
He moves in front of her and spreads his hands,&nbsp;
accepting his defeat. The opposition Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:10.960
walks towards him with a knife and stabs him.&nbsp;
At last, Akira falls to the ground. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:16.560
after his death, the old man smiles and&nbsp;
claps for him in appreciation. Just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:22.000
Kumi’s hands are untied. She smiles while looking&nbsp;
at her husband’s body, clearly delighted with what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:27.840
just happened. More surprisingly, the man who&nbsp;
died in the first round, doctor Tomoda, the nurse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:33.280
and everyone else that Akira met during the game&nbsp;
arrives at the arena while clapping for him.
&nbsp;

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:38.640
Then, Akira gets up from the floor, confused as&nbsp;
to why he isn’t feeling any pain. It turns out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.120
that the knife he was stabbed with was fake.&nbsp;
It is then revealed that the game was a trick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:48.640
to get Akira out of his depressive episode and&nbsp;
make him play chess again. He had been in a worse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:53.200
mental condition since losing the last match&nbsp;
with Super blue. So, to help him get better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:02.160
the doctor with Kumi and the old man orchestrated&nbsp;
the entire game as a part of “shock” therapy. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.800
old man is actually the inventor of Super&nbsp;
blue. He wasn't happy that his creation had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:11.520
made a great chess player like Akira stop&nbsp;
playing. So to make up for his mistake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:17.040
he organized and funded the game. This entire&nbsp;
time, Akira was playing with Super blue who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:21.840
had been passing answers to the old man through&nbsp;
his earpiece. The man reveals that the computer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:27.440
couldn’t comprehend Akira’s self-sacrificing move,&nbsp;
because of which it has malfunctioned. Meaning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:33.360
that he has finally won a game against the Super&nbsp;
blue. The movie ends as Akira and his wife hug,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:38.480
while everyone else claps for them.
